{"title":"1989 APMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1f799c4c33162471cef7d36874617ec73a5245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, x_3, \\dots , x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"11\" /> be positive real numbers, and let\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca6be7651fe26a12313722971194d219ada7d447.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=x_1+x_2+x_3+\\cdots +x_n\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46421c8ab6f8fac7fe2bae3ce9e737b5abd64f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+x_1)(1+x_2)(1+x_3)\\cdots (1+x_n)\\leq 1+S+\\dfrac{S^2}{2!}+\\dfrac{S^3}{3!}+\\cdots +\\dfrac{S^n}{n!}\\]\" width=\"529\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 APMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that the equation\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da940e703ad8743177ca4119cdb112232b2431b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6(6a^2+3b^2+c^2)=5n^2\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>has no solutions in integers except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/3159e3ab09257e66de9ead6fb22cb3d03f287c6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c=n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 APMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4630a83ffe9cbce55a4b12c292998213c827d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,A_2,A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> be three points in the plane, and for convenience, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/7822e3a6ca4a0b3127f98b689eb6d5e89e18f160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_4=A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e870106da48c163b283226b6beea1043254db19c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_5=A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea2046ce22518215ccd2ae54a008b594d8fd59b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1, 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be2b1de79fff66db67de3b18303bdd2912b7ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04d71635082231ff344631358090f79b2331853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_nA_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, and suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e173907ca992482385a50c6f62ede920362b1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/5081cacf883ceab9d84cff253970cb3d4501ba82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_nB_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f98691e15815d57434e3271c4749bfedf076944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_nC_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad9e854328448b0df262d95071c9a3e2cb8ca1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_nA_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2eacbcb991af87d495f8689ac0e952b51317dbaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, and that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43c42635c4b49e508bf28afec2c0d93921b9b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_nB_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/5/c356a1d06d4f4c1d931146aebd8f561696e2509a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_nA_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3cbf9ab1e976e485e5a8b8459491ffa0b561dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />. Calculate the ratio of the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e90a06cac65ce0ebc3ad5b2f510da7440b8c1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_1D_2D_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> to the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e158c78b12df3d413f8b0014cc67be81e97f3e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1E_2E_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 APMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a set consisting of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> of positive integers with the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d297b9cb790cb25703ad89c7948235dccd1f8c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq a&lt;b\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />. Show that there are at least \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19becf99931b8bfc253e6380b9c1305ffc93a7ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4m\\cdot \\dfrac{\\left(m-\\dfrac{n^2}{4}\\right)}{3n}\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p>triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a53387373f79f3f15a70abeeb58639c7d60aa2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fe40b98e74737c70752abaa29332bc3369bfd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> belong to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 APMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is a strictly increasing real-valued function on reals. It has inverse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/74153d34ed1e2096b5c034cb85eff5a695b887c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />. Find all possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65897b4cd42bb9cb48fb78a6f8ed1f8b87935910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+f&#39;(x)=2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 APMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_APMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asian_Pacific_Mathematics_Olympiad\" title=\"Asian Pacific Mathematics Olympiad\">Asian Pacific Mathematics Olympiad</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=APMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"APMO Problems and Solutions\">APMO Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 207/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6641/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6701:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195945 and revision id 78003. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}